From: Stefane Fermigier <sf@abilian.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:54:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 81/82] OdfFile reader: a section's properties are written in
 the schema's order

w:sectPr's children come from several functions, each writing its own:
columns and line numbering, then the section type, then the header and
footer references, then page size and margins. The schema wants them
interleaved, type after the references and before the page size:
1 509 of LibreOffice's ODF test documents. They are now sorted by the
schema's sequence once written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
